    "narrative": "Our strongest plays today are headlined by **Seiya Suzuki** (70.99) and **Corbin Carroll** (70.82), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs exceeding 4.25. **Seiya Suzuki** remains our most reliable asset today, fueled by an optimal #2 spot in the order and a favorable park factor, while **Corbin Carroll** is a mandatory start given our desperate need for stolen base production; despite a platoon disadvantage against Freeland, his upside remains elite. **Mickey Moniak** (67.47) and **Josh Naylor** (67.39) also emerge as core contributors. **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime position to capitalize on a massive 14% park-factor boost against Soroka, while **Josh Naylor** provides a high-floor profile against a hittable Javier, further bolstered by dynamic platoon advantages.\n\nThe decision to bench **Isaac Paredes** (47.46) was the most difficult call of the morning, as he hovered near our marginal threshold but ultimately fell victim to a tough matchup against Gilbert. While **Isaac Paredes** projected well enough to potentially see the field, the superior efficiency of **Cole Young** and **Brice Turang**\u2014despite their own platoon challenges\u2014pushed him to the pine to preserve game caps. We are also monitoring the status of **Jose Caballero**, who remains benched due to a lack of confirmed starting status; should he find his way into the lineup, he remains our primary contingency option for speed.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding **Brice Turang** (50.63) and **Moises Ballesteros** (52.68). **Brice Turang** faces the sternest test of our starters, as he squares off against the elite arm of Wheeler, necessitating a lower efficiency expectation despite his high-leverage order spot. Similarly, **Moises Ballesteros** faces a platoon disadvantage against Basso that limits his ceiling. We will keep a close eye on weather developments, though no immediate risks have been flagged that would force a pivot away from **Vinnie Pasquantino** (53.49) or **Austin Riley** (62.89) in their respective favorable park conditions. With **James Wood** (60.97) leading off in a high-xwOBA environment, we are well-positioned to maintain our offensive momentum.",
